:"0c8e91fc3a8b91af291fc93d972538f30352b049","position":"1795382784570444001-a883b802-6f36-404d-b7a0-6f48200ef2fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"97a2d5a4d5cd59e2075308e7ae3b87d3722c6872066d20932e4cad1989829969","event_uuid":"79efdaf3-d9a7-44c1-8aa9-59ba3863f56f","position":{"commit_sha":"78239d44b72fb49264dfcdb91ac6a5dcf3c54c33","position":"1795382882619104001-79efdaf3-d9a7-44c1-8aa9-59ba3863f56f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"220cea74fe13c2a840afa3a984922a0868a4bbd141fdf1e9f00b604cd122dab0","event_uuid":"17e623d5-615c-48d2-9175-c94f1dcdcdb1","position":{"commit_sha":"78239d44b72fb49264dfcdb91ac6a5dcf3c54c33","position":"1795382908469062001-17e623d5-615c-48d2-9175-c94f1dcdcdb1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"419bccc7410d92500aa2d7a25338ada76ab7c0a2bd4fa175071d223d75140a0c","event_uuid":"89c978c1-8cb8-4cfd-803f-944d6aff646b","position":{"commit_sha":"6a8b6ec32be3d9d6961eebbc6645b298b11a41cf","position":"1795384257193521001-89c978c1-8cb8-4cfd-803f-944d6aff646b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Findings and implementation (commit 4bf065d8ac4, not yet pushed)\n\nPre-fix CloudWatch evidence, 1-minute Sum of rebar/host:voter_errors on 2026-11-21 (PST): 06:15 = 1 (boto3 at the 06:15:50 error), 06:20 = 1 (probe), 06:35 = 1 (boto3 at 06:35:51), 06:36 = 1 (probe). 2 VOTER_ERROR markers in the journal, 4 counts.\n\nMetrics published by both review-bot code and observability.sh:\n- voter_errors: both, both dimensionless. Double-counted. Fixed: voter.py no longer publishes it.\n- review_bot_merge_change_errors: both. The probe publishes it dimensionless (the stream rebar-review-bot-merge-change-errors watches); voter_merge.py published it with a `reason` dimension, which CloudWatch keeps as separate streams, so the alarm stream was not doubled. No alarm, dashboard or doc reads the reason-tagged stream. Fixed anyway so the probe is the single publisher; the reason stays in the MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR journal record.\n- review_bot_artifact_emit_errors: only artifact_emit.py publishes it; the probe has no ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR section and no alarm reads it. Not double-counted; kept, docstring corrected.\n- review_bot_llm_* token metrics: only voter.py; kept.\n\nGuard test tests/unit/test_review_bot_single_metric_publisher.py reads both probe publishing shapes (`--metric-name <name>` and `publish_autodeploy_marker_delta '<re>' <name>`), finds MetricName values anywhere in a review-bot module that calls put_metric_data (including lists built before the call and f-string prefixes), and fails on any name it cannot resolve. Run against origin/main's voter.py and voter_merge.py it reports voter_errors and review_bot_merge_change_errors; on the fix it passes. ADR 0009 §Observability updated to match.","timestamp":1795384257193521001}],"created_at":1795380365117448001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bda2914d-73c5-4fb1-8e0f-e5fee7c8eb70","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ea5d-4932-8554-4544"},{"link_uuid":"ff7954bc-4942-4c3e-b85f-d8d4061b8d0f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"688f-060e-c96c-4484"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe `rebar/host:voter_errors` metric counts every `VOTER_ERROR` twice. `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py::_publish_voter_error_metric` (around lines 111-125) publishes `voter_errors = 1` through boto3 from inside the review-bot container at the moment of the error. Its comment assumes that publish usually fails for lack of credentials, but on the box the container resolves the instance role (metadata hop limit 2), so it succeeds. `infra/scripts/observability.sh` §4 (around lines 960-980) then counts the same journald marker on its next 5-minute run. Each error lands as 2 datapoints, usually in adjacent 5-minute periods.\n\nOn 2026-11-21, 2 isolated review timeouts (06:15:50 and 06:35:51 PST, both \"review timed out after 1200.0s\") made 3 breaching periods, and `rebar-gerrit-voter-errors` (Sum > 0 in 3 of 6 five-minute periods) went to ALARM at 06:36 and 06:51 PST. With the probe's counts alone, only 2 periods breach and neither ALARM occurs. That breaks the calibration set by enstatite-daemonic-tern: a lone timeout that recovers by itself must not page.\n\n`src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py::_publish_artifact_emit_error_metric` has the same pattern for `review_bot_artifact_emit_errors`; whether it double-counts has not been checked.\n\n## Findings before the change\nMetric names published by both review-bot code (`put_metric_data` in `src/rebar/review_bot/`) and `infra/scripts/observability.sh`, read from the tree at 39d78c81fd5:\n- `voter_errors`: both. `voter.py::_publish_voter_error_metric` and probe §4 (dimensionless). Double-counted.\n- `review_bot_merge_change_errors`: both. `voter_merge.py::publish_merge_change_error_metric` publishes it with a `reason` dimension; probe §4c publishes it dimensionless. CloudWatch keeps the two dimension sets as separate streams, so the dimensionless stream that `rebar-review-bot-merge-change-errors` (monitoring_88ab.tf) watches is counted once, but a second, reason-tagged stream exists that no alarm, dashboard or doc reads (grep over infra/, docs/, src/, tests/).\n- `review_bot_artifact_emit_errors`: only `artifact_emit.py`. The probe has no `ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR` section and no alarm reads the metric, so it is not double-counted.\n- `review_bot_llm_*` token metrics: only `voter.py`; the probe does not publish them.\nCloudWatch evidence (1-minute Sum of `rebar/host:voter_errors`, 2026-11-21): the 06:15:50 PST error produced 1 at 06:15 (boto3) and 1 at 06:20 (probe); the 06:35:51 PST error produced 1 at 06:35 and 1 at 06:36. 2 errors, 4 counts.\n\n## Approach\nMake the host probe the single publisher for every metric it already counts from a journald marker. The probe reads the marker from the journal with a persisted cursor, so it does not depend on container credentials and cannot be bypassed; the in-container boto3 publish is the redundant path.\n1. Delete `_publish_voter_error_metric` from `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` and its call in `_voter_error`. The `VOTER_ERROR {json}` stderr marker stays exactly as it is; it is the probe's input.\n2. Delete `publish_merge_change_error_metric` from `src/rebar/review_bot/voter_merge.py` and its call in `merge_change_error`. The `reason` stays in the `MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR` journal record, so the per-reason breakdown remains available from the journal; no consumer of the reason-tagged CloudWatch stream exists.\n3. Keep `_publish_artifact_emit_error_metric` in `artifact_emit.py`: it is the only publisher. Correct its docstring, which claims the host probe is the reliable path when the probe does not count that marker.\n4. Keep `_publish_token_usage_metrics`: it is the only publisher of `review_bot_llm_*`.\n5. Update the comment on `observability.sh` §4/§4c to say the probe is the only publisher. `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` and `monitoring_88ab.tf` already describe the probe as the publisher and stay unchanged (no Terraform change, no apply).\nNo new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` — remove the voter_errors boto3 publish.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/voter_merge.py` — remove the merge-change boto3 publish; update docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py` — docstring correction only.\n- `infra/scripts/observability.sh` — comment in §4/§4c naming the probe as the single publisher.\n- `tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py` — drop the stubs for the deleted helpers.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot_single_metric_publisher.py` — new guard test.\n\n## Testing\n- New guard test `tests/unit/test_review_bot_single_metric_publisher.py`: parse every `src/rebar/review_bot/**/*.py` with `ast`, collect each string `MetricName` passed in a `put_metric_data` call (literal names, and f-string prefixes), parse `observability.sh` for every `--metric-name <name>` it publishes, and assert the intersection is empty. Failure/edge cases: a positive self-test on a synthetic module that does publish `voter_errors` proves the scanner detects the overlap (so an empty result is not a blind scanner); a self-test that the probe parser finds `voter_errors` and `review_bot_merge_change_errors` in the real script (so a parsing regression cannot make the intersection trivially empty).\n- Existing `tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py` keeps asserting exactly 1 anchored marker line per error with and without logging configured.\n- `make verify` before push.\n- Box check after deploy: 1-minute `voter_errors` datapoints for the next natural `VOTER_ERROR` in the review-bot journal sum to exactly 1. No error is induced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One `VOTER_ERROR` produces exactly 1 count of `voter_errors` in CloudWatch, verified on the box against 1-minute datapoints.\n- [ ] Only `observability.sh` publishes `voter_errors`.\n- [ ] `review_bot_artifact_emit_errors` likewise has a single publisher, or a recorded finding shows it is not double-counted.\n- [ ] A test fails if review-bot code calls `put_metric_data` for a metric that the host probe also publishes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","reason":"remove the voter_errors boto3 publish"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/voter_merge.py","reason":"remove the review_bot_merge_change_errors boto3 publish"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py","reason":"correct the publisher docstring"},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"comment naming the probe as single publisher"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py","reason":"drop stubs of deleted helpers"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot_single_metric_publisher.py","reason":"new guard test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","688f-060e-c96c-4484"],["relates_to","ea5d-4932-8554-4544"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"79efdaf3-d9a7-44c1-8aa9-59ba3863f56f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ab02-9eaa-5b93-4c1f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"voter_errors double-counts every VOTER_ERROR (review-bot boto3 publish plus host probe), so 2 isolated timeouts page rebar-gerrit-voter-errors","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e62ac4b6-1368-4122-ae40-c2f3edbdb6ef","bda2914d-73c5-4fb1-8e0f-e5fee7c8eb70","ff7954bc-4942-4c3e-b85f-d8d4061b8d0f","75f38b48-6184-420d-987c-dea842586462","dfac812c-9e57-47af-b64c-5c48a538a508","a883b802-6f36-404d-b7a0-6f48200ef2fb","79efdaf3-d9a7-44c1-8aa9-59ba3863f56f","17e623d5-615c-48d2-9175-c94f1dcdcdb1","89c978c1-8cb8-4cfd-803f-944d6aff646b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795384257193521002,"uuid":"f9e9569e-fdb6-47d9-bd70-8e834b9d4b12"}